{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T17:28:12.831Z","data":{"text":"Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Scoped changes (4 files):**\n\n1. **`package.json`** — bumped `version` to `0.1.0`, added `test:e2e` script (`node --import tsx --test \"tests/e2e/**/*.e2e.ts\"`). No dependency/lockfile change.\n\n2. **`tests/release.test.ts`** (new, offline) — asserts `version` is `0.1.0` and the exact `test:e2e` script, and that in-process `paas --version` prints `0.1.0\\n` with empty stderr and exit 0.\n\n3. **`tests/e2e/first-deploy.e2e.ts`** (new) — skips one `first real deploy` test without `PAAS_E2E=1`; with it, refuses to run when `paas-caddy` exists (touching nothing), otherwise drives the CLI in-process against a socket-resolved `DockerRuntime` labelled `paas.test=e2e` through all seven steps (up → create → deploy → blue GET → green redeploy with continuous 100 ms polling asserting every status 200 → logs → stop → ingress down). `after` removes labelled resources and the temp `PAAS_HOME` in a `finally`.\n\n4. **`README.md`** — added the \"Quickstart\" section after \"Requirements\" with Docker Desktop and Rootless Podman subsections, low-port caveat, `.localhost` note, manual-testing pointer, updated Status, and marked roadmap item 10 done.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Task verify: 2 passed, 1 skipped, exit 0.\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify`): 391 passed, typecheck clean.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/012-first-real-deploy/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nOne note: the `PAAS_E2E=1` branch requires a real engine, which the proposal treats as a human step, so only the skip path/typecheck/offline assertions ran here."}}
